-- 150: Replace all bill reminder data with the "Priyank Sir Bills Due
-- Dated 27th Sept, 2026" dataset (Sheet3).
--
-- Replaces the migration 124 seed. That seed only ever wrote the
-- *_date_display free-text columns, so due_date / renewal_date /
-- frequency_type were NULL on every row: the Renewal Date column rendered
-- blank, derivedStatus was stuck on "Upcoming", and the cron in
-- services/reminderNotificationScheduler.js could not alert on anything.
-- This migration writes real dates and recurrence fields.
--
-- Generated by scripts/gen_reminder_seed_150.mjs - do not hand edit.
-- Source: "Priyank Sir Bills Due Dated 27th Sept, 2026.xlsx", Sheet3.
--   102 bill lines seeded; the sheet does not fill every cell:
--     54  carry a real due date
--     36  are label + billing-cycle only (no date/payment/note), because
--          the sheet leaves them empty under sub-headings like Mobile Recharge,
--          Finance, Loan EMI, Income Tax, Rent TDS and Advance Tax
--     12  have payment or period detail but no parseable due date
--   31 rows have no owner. The undated rows keep nulls rather than
--   invented values, so they render with a blank Due Date and an
--   "Upcoming" status, and the cron will never alert on them. Fill them in
--   from the Reminder form once the real dates are known.
-- Each row carries source_section (its sheet sub-heading), so the UI can
-- render all 27 sub-headings and the dedupe keeps the 18 sparse Finance
-- rows (Income Tax / Advance Tax / Accounts and Audit Fees) distinct.
-- Sheet1 (61 rows) and Sheet2 (79 rows) are older partial drafts: ignored.
-- Generated 2026-09-28 (recurring rules resolved from this date).
--
-- Safe to re-run. reminder_device_tokens is left alone: it holds the live
-- FCM token and is not tied to a reminder id. reminders_id_seq is not
-- reset, so the ids handed out to new reminders keep climbing past any
-- id the app has already cached.

BEGIN;

DELETE FROM reminder_alert_log;
DELETE FROM reminder_history;
DELETE FROM reminders;

ALTER TABLE reminders ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS source_section text;


COMMIT;
